   1045  fc4c							; Room-exit handlers — MOVED from bank0 (C3, 2026-10-20; were $F4DB-$F535 = 90 B).
   1046  fc4c							; Connections are 2 nibble-packed bytes per room (up<<4|down, left<<4|right) at
   1047  fc4c							; level base + 2n = bank2 level data, so each handler reads its own record
   1048  fc4c							; directly: the bank1 `CallPad_GetConnIdx` hop AND the `jsr FoldIndirect` hop
   1049  fc4c							; are gone (cold path, so cycles do not matter, but 2 switches/crossing do).
   1050  fc4c							; Entry: bank0's `jsr ExitRoomXxx` pad ($FBD9-$FBE4, `sta $1FF8`) -> the `jmp`
   1051  fc4c							; halves at $FBDC-$FBE5 above. Every exit path ends in a `jmp`:
   1052  fc4c							;   * no exit	    -> ReturnPad (bank0 `rts` pops the caller's jsr frame)
   1053  fc4c							;   * room changed -> `jmp EnterRoomB2`, whose own `jmp ReturnPad` does the same
   1054  fc4c							; The opposite-edge placement is written BEFORE EnterRoomB2 because EnterRoom
   1055  fc4c							; never reads/writes RoomX/RoomY (verified in EnterRoomB2 + B3RoomBlocks), and
   1056  fc4c							; Y is used for the constant so A keeps the ROOM INDEX EnterRoomB2 stores.
   1057  fc4c							; Guard: verify_build.check_exit_handlers.
   1058  fc4c							; ==============================================================================
